From 7b196670ccdad2fa2155fb24775d65fc13718a7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:57:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Origin chats: a done replica card pending release
 reads done_pending_release, not unknown

Problem: origin chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6 (laptop-1, kanban.sync.links_reader=replica), 2026-11-13
08:34-08:36 PST. Freshly finished worker cards (t_01a1d5ad588a78e9, t_01a1d5c0c1d54f8d, t_01a1d5c039be0093)
were listed `unknown` by `hermes kanban chat-tasks` for 1-2 min, and the ask-gate showed one to David as
`[unknown]` in "Cards linked to this chat". Row: reported_status done, source replica, released false.

Why 1: `kanban_chat_links.replica_cards` labels every unreleased link to a closed card `unknown`
(`unknown = missing or status in TERMINAL_STATUSES or status is None`), whatever the card's reported status.
Why 2: the owner releases a chat link only after it has verified the completion, on its next reconcile
pass; the replica carries the card's `done` one or two sync passes earlier. In that window the link is
unreleased, so the card read `unknown` although its state was known: done, release pending.
Why 3: one label served two states: "state unknown" (no card row, no status, archived without a completion)
and "done, release not verified yet". Readers (`_replica_bucket`, parked/stalled counts, `session_tasks`,
`_ledger_obligation`, ledger fallback, notice_fanout) only needed "closed and unfinished", which `unknown` +
`unfinished` stood for.
Root (happened): no distinct state for a done card whose release is pending; `unknown` was the only
fail-closed bucket. (`missing_qualified_identity` on the row is the card's execution observation, a
liveness field of a closed card; it does not drive the status.)
Root (not caught): the tests pinned the conflation (`..._stays_an_unknown_chip_and_counts`) and checked
counts/parity only, never the label a reader shows for a done card mid-release.
Recurrence: first time for the label; same window as the 19 hub cards of chat 20261026_170127_f07c32.

Fix:
- `kanban_session_activity_release`: `DONE_PENDING_RELEASE`, `PENDING_RELEASE_STATUSES` (unknown +
  done_pending_release) and `unreleased_obligation(card)`.
- `replica_cards`: an unreleased link whose card row reports `done` reads `done_pending_release`; a missing
  row, no status or `archived` stay `unknown`. Still `unfinished: True, released: False`: counted, listed and
  never released until the owner releases the link.
- Every reader of the "closed, unfinished" bucket accepts both labels (sidebar bucket, parked, stalled
  exclusion, session_tasks listing, `_ledger_obligation`, ledger fallback, notice_fanout's remote change pass).
- The origin-ledger path (links_reader=ledger) is unchanged: it still labels these `unknown`.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_pending_release.py (done -> pending -> released one pass
later; never-verified stays pending and counted; missing/None/archived stay unknown) and
tests/tui_gateway/test_remote_card_outcomes.py::test_done_pending_release_stays_observed_until_released
fail on origin/main (4 failed) and pass here; 5 existing assertions moved from `unknown` to the new label.
152 test files touching these modules: 2536 passed.
